# Peer-to-peer task-transfer negotiation message, part of the PROPOSE_TASK_TRANSFER
# family of actions. Published on the shared /fleet/agent/task_transfer topic by
# every decentralized_agent - there is no central negotiation broker, matching the
# decentralized claim protocol.
#
# Every message belongs to exactly one conversation_id, generated by the initiator.
# A full negotiation is one of:
#   OFFER -> BID/COUNTER_PROPOSAL (one or more) -> ACCEPT (to winner) + REJECT (to
#            losers) -> COMMIT (broadcast, final record)
#   OFFER -> (no bids within the deadline) -> TIMEOUT (broadcast)
# so the complete history of any transfer - who proposed it, who bid, who won, when -
# is reconstructable purely from the ordered sequence of messages sharing one
# conversation_id (negotiations.csv via event_logger_node.py). This is what makes the
# protocol auditable from proposal to execution.

string conversation_id
string performative     # OFFER | BID | COUNTER_PROPOSAL | ACCEPT | REJECT | COMMIT | TIMEOUT
string from_robot_id
string to_robot_id      # empty = broadcast (OFFER, TIMEOUT, COMMIT); addressed for BID/ACCEPT/REJECT
string station_name
string side             # "input" | "output"
float32 x
float32 y
float32 cost            # meaningful for OFFER (initiator's own cost) and BID/COUNTER_PROPOSAL
string reason_code      # e.g. "LOW_BATTERY"
builtin_interfaces/Time stamp
